            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did haṁsaḥ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तर्हि",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तर्हि (tarhi) — \"then, in that case\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तर्हि (tarhi) — \"then, in that case\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said on its own it answers a condition. Somebody tells you how matters stand; तर्हि (tarhi) is your \"then, all right\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is built on the same t- that points for you in तत् and in तत्र. Those two point at a thing and at a place; तर्हि (tarhi) points at a moment — at that time, and so, therefore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A one-word answer to how things stand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
